<problem>
<!-- <title>differentiate cubic plus parameter</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="aa" from="1" to=" 7" />
<selectFromSequence name="bb" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="true" from="-5" to=" 5" />

<selectFromSequence name="dd" from="2" to=" 10" />
<select name="x"> x y z t</select>
<select name="par"> a b c m n</select>
<select name="f"> f g h</select>

<selectFromSequence name="pow" from="2" to="5" />
<math name="answer" simplify="full">3*$aa *$x ^2+2*$bb[1] *$x +$bb[2] </math>
<math name="fun" simplify="full">$aa *$x ^3 + $bb[1] *$x ^2 + $bb[2] *$x  + $dd *$par ^$pow </math>
<select name="deriv">
  <option>
    <math>d$f / d$x</math>
  </option>
  <option>
    <math referencesAreFunctionSymbols="$f">$f'($x)</math>
  </option>
</select>

<select name="wording">1 2 3 4 5</select>
</setup>


<conditionalContent>
  <case condition="$wording=1">
    <p>Given that $par is a constant parameter, compute the derivative, <m>$deriv[1][1] </m>, of
    <me>$f($x) = $fun.</me>
    <m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$answer</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=2">
  <p>Calculate the derivative of
    <me>$f($x) = $fun,</me>
    where $par is a constant parameter.</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$answer</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=3">
  <p>For the function
    <me>$f($x) = $fun,</me>
    what is the derivative $deriv[1][1]?  View $par as a constant parameter.</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$answer</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=4">
  <p>Let <m>$f($x) = $fun.</m>  What is the derivative of <m>$f($x)</m>?  The quantity $par is a constant parameter.</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$answer</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=5">
  <p>The function <m>$f($x) = $fun</m> involves a constant parameter $par.  Calculate the derivative $deriv[1][1].</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$answer</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
</conditionalContent>




<solution>
The only trick to calculate this derivative is what to do about the term <m>$dd $par ^$pow </m> with the constant parameter <m>$par </m>.  Since the constant number <m>$dd $par ^$pow </m> is added to the function, and the derivative of a constant is zero, the term <m>$dd $par ^$pow </m> just adds zero to the derivative.  The derivative of <m>$f </m> is
<me>$deriv[1][1] =$answer </me>

</solution>


</problem>